From 4726e89697eb7d6a595d1624019beb0cb38c00cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:26:18 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] strings: the comments of five core strings name their
 translation in Estuary

The comment of a core string of a setting of Hades says where it is translated
("translated in Estuary (#n)"), which is what a translator reads and what the check of the
pairs of strings follows. Those of HDR at more than 8 bits on NVIDIA (41011, 41012, read
from Estuary 32510 and 32511 since d1968dc) and of the notice of the playback mode
(41101 to 41103: 32502 to 32504) did not say it. Only comments of the file change.

Host test (outside the tree): pairs.py of the integration (every label and help of a
setting of Hades has an Estuary twin with the same English and a Spanish text) said 4
errors, these, and says none.
---
 addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po | 10 +++++-----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
index 9cef5c3..de32cf5 100644
--- a/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
+++ b/addons/resource.language.en_gb/resources/strings.po
@@ -27136,13 +27136,13 @@ msgctxt "#41010"
 msgid "The sound of {} comes back with the next video that changes the display mode, or after restarting Hades"
 msgstr ""
 
-#. Hades: label of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most (NVIDIA)
+#. Hades: label of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most (NVIDIA); translated in Estuary (#32510)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#41011"
 msgid "HDR at more than 8 bits where the card sends RGB at 8 (NVIDIA)"
 msgstr ""
 
-#. Hades: help of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most
+#. Hades: help of the setting of HDR at more than 8 bits where the graphics send RGB at 8 bits at most; translated in Estuary (#32511)
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
 msgctxt "#41012"
 msgid "For older NVIDIA cards (GeForce GTX 10 and GTX 16, RTX 20, TITAN V) that send RGB at only 8 bits over HDMI. On: HDR goes out in a format that carries 10 or 12 bits (YCbCr 4:2:2) where the TV and the picture mode allow it, which reduces banding. Where they do not, HDR goes out as before. Dolby Vision and SDR are not affected. Off until this is confirmed on those cards. Takes effect from the next video."
@@ -27150,19 +27150,19 @@ msgstr ""
 
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. label of setting "videoscreen.hadesplaybackmode"
+#. label of setting "videoscreen.hadesplaybackmode"; translated in Estuary (#32502)
 msgctxt "#41101"
 msgid "Show the playback mode when a video starts"
 msgstr ""
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. help of setting "videoscreen.hadesplaybackmode"
+#. help of setting "videoscreen.hadesplaybackmode"; translated in Estuary (#32503)
 msgctxt "#41102"
 msgid "Shows a short notice a moment after a video starts, with the mode it plays in: for example 'Dolby Vision · FEL · 3840x2160 @ 23.976 Hz', or 'Dolby Vision → HDR10' where a Dolby Vision video is sent as HDR10. It is shown once per video. Off by default. The player information shows every detail."
 msgstr ""
 
 #: system/settings/settings.xml
-#. heading of the notice of the playback mode
+#. heading of the notice of the playback mode; translated in Estuary (#32504)
 msgctxt "#41103"
 msgid "Playback mode"
 msgstr ""
-- 
